2. Because smulh (and similarly add) require that the destination and first source be the same register, we first make a copy of the true index (in z0.s) into z2.s and then do
  smulh z2.s, p0/m, z2.s, z0.s
3. Finally, we add the shifted value back into z0.s using an “in‐place” add:
  add z0.s, p0/m, z0.s, z2.s

