Explanation of changes in memcpy (and similarly in memset):
  • ld1d and st1d now use the extended predicate “p0/z” so that inactive lanes become zero.
  • The lsl, mls and movprfx instructions now use “p0/m” (merging predicate) as required.
  • The “and” instruction now uses an immediate of 0xFFFFFFFFFFFFFFFF (which is a valid SVE logical immediate)
    so that z1 remains zero.

This version should compile and link directly with a standard AArch64+SVE assembler/compiler.

