Explanation of the two key changes:
1. In the odd branch of powm the original instruction
    asr w8, x8, #36
was invalid because the immediate 36 cannot be used when the destination is a 32‐bit register. Instead we do:
  asr x8, x8, #36
  mov w8, x8
which shifts a 64‐bit register by 36 places and then passes the proper 32‐bit value onward.
2. In memcpy the “and” instruction has been changed from
  and z1.d, z1.d, #-1
to
  and z1.d, z1.d, #0xffffffffffffffff
so that the immediate is legal (a 64‐bit constant having a contiguous run of ones).

This version should compile and link on an AArch64 system with SVE enabled.

