• For CNTW use p0.s rather than p0 (i.e. “cntw x3, p0.s, #1”).
• For INDEX the second “stride” operand must be an immediate in the allowed range (–16 to 15); so remove the register‐based version and use “index z0.s, #0, #1”.
• For LSR include the merge modifier (“p0/m”).
• For CNTH use p0.h.
• For MUL the immediate form requires that the destination equal the first source. Therefore copy z1 to z2, then do “mul z2.s, z2.s, #3”.
• For RDVL the immediate must lie in –32…31. Since we want to compute VL × 32 (and RDVL actually computes (imm+1)×VL bytes), we use an immediate of 31.
