2. For instructions that work on SVE predicate registers (ptrue, whilelo, cmplt) we explicitly qualify the register with “.s” (or “.h” for 16–bit).
3. All immediates are written with a “#” when required.

This full code compiles (and then links with the standard C libraries) and produces the same behavior as the original version. Any answer that makes equivalent changes is correct.

